    {
      "type": "context",
      "id": "CXJlS",
      "x": 11079,
      "y": 2859,
      "width": 330,
      "height": 303,
      "content": "for \"Coming Soon\" items, the muted text + chip combo is doing two things well: the \"Coming Soon\" chip tells users why it's not active, while the dimmed text lets their eye skip past it when scanning for current features. If you restore full contrast, those items compete visually with actionable ones, and users might click expecting functionality. The current treatment is the best of both — it communicates status without hiding what's on the roadmap."
    },
